<section id="sources"><h2>Sources and editorial notes</h2><p>This guide is written for English-speaking readers and distinguishes publication facts from interpretations of the poem. Its account of the plot and historical context is informed by the following institutional sources:</p><ul><li><a href="https://www.cervantesvirtual.com/portales/jose_hernandez/obra/el-gaucho-martin-fierro--0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Biblioteca Virtual Miguel de Cervantes — bibliographic record for the 1872 edition</a>.</li><li><a href="https://www.teatrocervantes.gob.ar/obra/el-martin-fierro/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Teatro Nacional Cervantes — literary and narrative overview of both parts</a>.</li><li><a href="https://www.educ.ar/recursos/131417/emel-gaucho-martin-fierroem-de-jose-hernandez" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Educ.ar — introduction to El gaucho Martín Fierro and its social themes</a>.</li><li><a href="/archivo/">MARTINFIERRO.ORG historical archive (currently in Spanish)</a>.</li></ul><p><strong>Editorial distinction:</strong> The guide contains modern English prose about the work, not a published English translation of the poem. Names of the original Spanish editions are retained.</p></section>
